{
  "protocol": "tls",
  "title": "TLS 1.2 handshake record",
  "source": "RFC 5246 §6.2 (record), §7.4.1 (hellos); RFC 8446 §4.1.2 (why 1.3 looks the same here)",
  "nodes": [
    {
      "id": "tls",
      "kind": "protocol",
      "about": [
        "TLS 1.2 — RFC 5246 §6.2 (the record) and §7.4.1 (the hellos).",
        "",
        "Three lengths, one inside the next: a record says how many octets its fragment is, a handshake",
        "message says how many its body is, and the extensions block says how many all the extensions",
        "come to. Two of them are two octets and the middle one is THREE, which is the whole reason a",
        "width is a parameter of a form rather than a set of named integer kinds.",
        "",
        "And the thing TLS is made of, which no other protocol here has: a VECTOR. A length in octets",
        "followed by items of one kind with no tag on them — eight cipher suites in sixteen octets, four",
        "groups in eight. Nothing counts them; the reading spends the length. Which is the same machinery",
        "as a run of extensions, where the items are NOT all the same width, and that is the point: the",
        "description says where the run ends, not how many things are in it.",
        "",
        "One message rather than two, forking in the middle. A ClientHello and a ServerHello share a",
        "record header, a message header, a version, a random and a session id, then differ, then share an",
        "extensions block — and what they differ in is not a field's value but its SHAPE: the client",
        "offers a vector of suites and a vector of compression methods, the server picks one of each and",
        "writes it as a plain number. Same name in the specification, different thing on the wire, so two",
        "nodes. The fork reads the message type that was read four octets earlier — no look-ahead, because",
        "nothing has to be looked at twice.",
        "",
        "An extension's data is octets. That is not a shortcut: RFC 5246 §7.4.1.4 says an implementation",
        "MUST ignore an extension it does not recognise, and IANA's registry grows. A description that",
        "forked on the extension type would refuse every extension invented after it was written, which",
        "is the one thing this format is built to survive. What the octets of server_name or ALPN mean is",
        "a layer above, and the shape for it already exists — an extension body is exactly what a carried",
        "sub-protocol is.",
        "",
        "Scope, stated in the octets rather than here. The content type is checked to be handshake: an",
        "application_data record's body is AEAD ciphertext, and there is nothing to describe until a key",
        "exists, which is not something a message format has. The record version is checked to be TLS 1.0",
        "or 1.2, so SSL 3.0 is refused. The message type is checked to be a hello, so a Certificate or a",
        "Finished in the same record is refused rather than read as a hello with implausible fields.",
        "",
        "What it does NOT refuse, and this is worth stating because it looks like an omission: a TLS 1.3",
        "hello. RFC 8446 §4.1.2 keeps legacy_version at 0x0303 and moves the real one into an extension,",
        "so a 1.3 hello has this exact shape and reads correctly here. Which version was agreed is inside",
        "an extension's octets, and this does not look inside those."
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "record",
      "kind": "message",
      "as": "a handshake record",
      "about": "RFC 5246 §6.2.1. One record, carrying one handshake message."
    },
    {
      "id": "packing.record",
      "kind": "packing"
    },
    {
      "id": "constant.handshake",
      "kind": "constant",
      "holds": {
        "int": 22
      },
      "label": "handshake",
      "about": "RFC 5246 §6.2.1's ContentType. 20 is change_cipher_spec, 21 alert, 23 application_data."
    },
    {
      "id": "contentType",
      "kind": "field",
      "as": "Content Type",
      "form": {
        "of": "run",
        "bits": 8
      },
      "about": "What this record carries. One of four, and this describes one of them."
    },
    {
      "id": "valid.handshake",
      "kind": "validator",
      "ranges": [
        {
          "from": {
            "int": 22
          },
          "to": {
            "int": 22
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "input.recordVersion",
      "kind": "input",
      "as": "Record Version",
      "gives": "Int",
      "purpose": "What goes in the record header, which is not necessarily what is being negotiated: RFC 5246 appendix E.1 has a client write 0x0301 on its first record whatever it means to offer."
    },
    {
      "id": "recordVersion",
      "kind": "field",
      "as": "Record Version",
      "form": {
        "of": "scalar",
        "octets": 2,
        "big": true,
        "signed": false
      },
      "about": "0x0301 on the client's first record and 0x0303 on the server's answer, in the corpus and in the wild. A version that a middlebox will not choke on, rather than a claim."
    },
    {
      "id": "evaluated.recordVersion",
      "kind": "evaluated",
      "label": "the version on the record",
      "runs": "given",
      "gives": "Int",
      "takes": {
        "given": "Int"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "valid.recordVersion",
      "kind": "validator",
      "ranges": [
        {
          "from": {
            "int": 769
          },
          "to": {
            "int": 769
          }
        },
        {
          "from": {
            "int": 771
          },
          "to": {
            "int": 771
          }
        }
      ],
      "about": "TLS 1.0's value and TLS 1.2's."
    },
    {
      "id": "recordLength",
      "kind": "field",
      "as": "Record Length",
      "form": {
        "of": "scalar",
        "octets": 2,
        "big": true,
        "signed": false
      },
      "about": "RFC 5246 §6.2.1 bounds this at 2^14. What it measures begins after it — unlike BACnet's BVLC length, which counts itself, and the difference between the two descriptions is which set the edge points at."
    },
    {
      "id": "evaluated.recordLength",
      "kind": "evaluated",
      "label": "octets of fragment",
      "runs": "held",
      "gives": "Int",
      "takes": {
        "held": "Int"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "fragment",
      "kind": "set",
      "as": "what the record carries",
      "about": "One handshake message, here. A real server coalesces several into one record and splits one across two, because the two framings are not aligned — nothing in a record says where a message ends, and nothing in a message says which record it came in."
    },
    {
      "id": "input.messageType",
      "kind": "input",
      "as": "Message Type",
      "gives": "Int",
      "purpose": "1 for a ClientHello, 2 for a ServerHello. What the two shapes are told apart by."
    },
    {
      "id": "messageType",
      "kind": "field",
      "as": "Handshake Type",
      "form": {
        "of": "run",
        "bits": 8
      },
      "about": "RFC 5246 §7.4. Read once, and read again by nothing: the fork later on asks this node what it came to rather than looking at the octet a second time."
    },
    {
      "id": "evaluated.messageType",
      "kind": "evaluated",
      "label": "which hello this is",
      "runs": "which",
      "gives": "Int",
      "takes": {
        "which": "Int"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "valid.messageType",
      "kind": "validator",
      "ranges": [
        {
          "from": {
            "int": 1
          },
          "to": {
            "int": 1
          }
        },
        {
          "from": {
            "int": 2
          },
          "to": {
            "int": 2
          }
        }
      ],
      "about": "client_hello and server_hello."
    },
    {
      "id": "handshakeLength",
      "kind": "field",
      "as": "Handshake Length",
      "form": {
        "of": "scalar",
        "octets": 3,
        "big": true,
        "signed": false
      },
      "about": "THREE octets, big-endian — RFC 5246 §7.4's uint24. The one place a length is not a power-of-two width, and the reason a form takes an octet count rather than a scalar being one of u8/u16/u32."
    },
    {
      "id": "evaluated.handshakeLength",
      "kind": "evaluated",
      "label": "octets of hello",
      "runs": "held",
      "gives": "Int",
      "takes": {
        "held": "Int"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "hello",
      "kind": "set",
      "as": "the hello",
      "about": "What the handshake length measures: everything after it, and neither the type nor the length in front of it."
    },
    {
      "id": "input.version",
      "kind": "input",
      "as": "Version",
      "gives": "Int",
      "purpose": "What is offered, or what was agreed. 0x0303 is TLS 1.2 — and also what a TLS 1.3 hello writes here, because RFC 8446 moved the real answer into an extension."
    },
    {
      "id": "version",
      "kind": "field",
      "as": "Version",
      "form": {
        "of": "scalar",
        "octets": 2,
        "big": true,
        "signed": false
      },
      "about": "RFC 5246 §7.4.1.2's client_version, §7.4.1.3's server_version. The same two octets in the same place meaning 'the best I can do' one way and 'what we are doing' the other — which is a difference in who is speaking, not in the message format."
    },
    {
      "id": "evaluated.version",
      "kind": "evaluated",
      "label": "the version in the hello",
      "runs": "given",
      "gives": "Int",
      "takes": {
        "given": "Int"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "input.random",
      "kind": "input",
      "as": "Random",
      "gives": "Bytes",
      "purpose": "Thirty-two octets. RFC 5246 §7.4.1.2 put a four-octet clock at the front of it and RFC 8446 §4.1.2 says fill the lot with randomness, so what is in it is the sender's business."
    },
    {
      "id": "random",
      "kind": "field",
      "as": "Random",
      "form": {
        "of": "opaque",
        "octets": 32
      },
      "about": "A fixed width, which makes it the only span here that no length field measures."
    },
    {
      "id": "evaluated.random",
      "kind": "evaluated",
      "label": "this hello's random",
      "runs": "given",
      "gives": "Bytes",
      "takes": {
        "given": "Bytes"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "sessionIdLength",
      "kind": "field",
      "as": "Session ID Length",
      "form": {
        "of": "scalar",
        "octets": 1,
        "big": true,
        "signed": false
      },
      "about": "One octet, because RFC 5246 §7.4.1.2 writes the field as opaque SessionID<0..32> and a vector's length prefix is as wide as its maximum needs."
    },
    {
      "id": "evaluated.sessionIdLength",
      "kind": "evaluated",
      "label": "octets of sessionId",
      "runs": "held",
      "gives": "Int",
      "takes": {
        "held": "Int"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "valid.sessionId",
      "kind": "validator",
      "ranges": [
        {
          "from": {
            "int": 0
          },
          "to": {
            "int": 32
          }
        }
      ],
      "about": "RFC 5246 §7.4.1.2: SessionID is 0 to 32 octets."
    },
    {
      "id": "input.sessionId",
      "kind": "input",
      "as": "Session ID",
      "gives": "Bytes",
      "purpose": "Empty when nothing is being resumed. A server that echoes the client's is resuming; a server that sends a different one is not — which is a comparison ACROSS two messages, so it is not in either of them."
    },
    {
      "id": "sessionId",
      "kind": "field",
      "as": "Session ID",
      "form": {
        "of": "opaque"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "evaluated.sessionId",
      "kind": "evaluated",
      "label": "this hello's session id",
      "runs": "given",
      "gives": "Bytes",
      "takes": {
        "given": "Bytes"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "evaluated.sessionIdExtent",
      "kind": "evaluated",
      "label": "octets of session id, from the length",
      "runs": "len",
      "gives": "Int",
      "takes": {
        "len": "Int"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "variant",
      "kind": "set",
      "as": "offered, or chosen",
      "about": [
        "The fork, and what it decides on is a field read four octets ago rather than octets looked at",
        "again.",
        "",
        "Both arms are inside what the handshake length measures, so the one not taken has to say it is",
        "NOT THERE — a span waiting on a member the walk stepped past waits for ever. That is what makes",
        "an arm optional rather than merely unreached."
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "offered",
      "kind": "set",
      "as": "what the client offers",
      "about": "RFC 5246 §7.4.1.2. Two vectors: every suite it will accept, in preference order, and every compression method — which is always the one that does nothing, and is still a vector."
    },
    {
      "id": "chosen",
      "kind": "set",
      "as": "what the server picked",
      "about": [
        "RFC 5246 §7.4.1.3, and the shape is the finding rather than the content.",
        "",
        "The specification calls the client's field cipher_suites and the server's cipher_suite, and the",
        "difference is not a plural: one is a length and a list and the other is two octets. Reading the",
        "server's answer with the client's description would take the first suite as a length. So they",
        "are different nodes, which is the same rule that made MQTT's CONNECT and CONNACK packet types",
        "two nodes rather than one with two legal values."
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "cipherSuitesLength",
      "kind": "field",
      "as": "Cipher Suites Length",
      "form": {
        "of": "scalar",
        "octets": 2,
        "big": true,
        "signed": false
      },
      "about": "In OCTETS, not in suites — sixteen for eight of them. Which is why nothing has to divide: the reading spends octets and stops when they are gone."
    },
    {
      "id": "evaluated.cipherSuitesLength",
      "kind": "evaluated",
      "label": "octets of cipherSuites",
      "runs": "held",
      "gives": "Int",
      "takes": {
        "held": "Int"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "cipherSuites",
      "kind": "set",
      "as": "the suites offered",
      "about": "A vector: items of one kind with nothing marking where one ends, because they are all two octets wide. The order is the client's preference and is therefore part of the message."
    },
    {
      "id": "input.cipherSuites",
      "kind": "input",
      "as": "Cipher Suites",
      "gives": "List",
      "of": "Int",
      "purpose": "Every suite the client will accept, best first."
    },
    {
      "id": "suite",
      "kind": "field",
      "as": "Cipher Suite",
      "form": {
        "of": "scalar",
        "octets": 2,
        "big": true,
        "signed": false
      },
      "about": "Two octets from a registry that has hundreds of entries and grows. Carried, not classified — which of them is acceptable is policy, and policy is not a message format."
    },
    {
      "id": "evaluated.suite",
      "kind": "evaluated",
      "label": "this suite",
      "runs": "item",
      "gives": "Int"
    },
    {
      "id": "compressionMethodsLength",
      "kind": "field",
      "as": "Compression Methods Length",
      "form": {
        "of": "scalar",
        "octets": 1,
        "big": true,
        "signed": false
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "evaluated.compressionMethodsLength",
      "kind": "evaluated",
      "label": "octets of compressionMethods",
      "runs": "held",
      "gives": "Int",
      "takes": {
        "held": "Int"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "compressionMethods",
      "kind": "set",
      "as": "the compression methods offered",
      "about": "One octet each, and in practice one of them holding zero. RFC 7457 §2.6 explains why anything else here is a vulnerability rather than a feature, and the vector survives because the format cannot be changed."
    },
    {
      "id": "input.compressionMethods",
      "kind": "input",
      "as": "Compression Methods",
      "gives": "List",
      "of": "Int",
      "purpose": "Always [0] in anything made this decade."
    },
    {
      "id": "compression",
      "kind": "field",
      "as": "Compression Method",
      "form": {
        "of": "scalar",
        "octets": 1,
        "big": true,
        "signed": false
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "evaluated.compression",
      "kind": "evaluated",
      "label": "this compression method",
      "runs": "item",
      "gives": "Int"
    },
    {
      "id": "input.chosenSuite",
      "kind": "input",
      "as": "Cipher Suite",
      "gives": "Int",
      "purpose": "The one suite the server picked."
    },
    {
      "id": "chosenSuite",
      "kind": "field",
      "as": "Cipher Suite",
      "form": {
        "of": "scalar",
        "octets": 2,
        "big": true,
        "signed": false
      },
      "about": "Two octets and no length, because there is one of it."
    },
    {
      "id": "evaluated.chosenSuite",
      "kind": "evaluated",
      "label": "the suite agreed",
      "runs": "given",
      "gives": "Int",
      "takes": {
        "given": "Int"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "input.chosenCompression",
      "kind": "input",
      "as": "Compression Method",
      "gives": "Int",
      "purpose": "The one method the server picked."
    },
    {
      "id": "chosenCompression",
      "kind": "field",
      "as": "Compression Method",
      "form": {
        "of": "scalar",
        "octets": 1,
        "big": true,
        "signed": false
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "evaluated.chosenCompression",
      "kind": "evaluated",
      "label": "the compression agreed",
      "runs": "given",
      "gives": "Int",
      "takes": {
        "given": "Int"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "extensionsLength",
      "kind": "field",
      "as": "Extensions Length",
      "form": {
        "of": "scalar",
        "octets": 2,
        "big": true,
        "signed": false
      },
      "about": "The third length in a row that measures a span the reading has to spend rather than count through — and the first whose items are NOT all the same width."
    },
    {
      "id": "evaluated.extensionsLength",
      "kind": "evaluated",
      "label": "octets of extensions",
      "runs": "held",
      "gives": "Int",
      "takes": {
        "held": "Int"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "extensions",
      "kind": "set",
      "as": "the extensions",
      "about": [
        "A run of them, ending where the length says. Each one is a type, a length, and that many octets.",
        "",
        "Their ORDER is on the wire and carries nothing — RFC 5246 §7.4.1.4 requires only that a type",
        "appear once. It is kept because a message that came in one order and went out in another is a",
        "different message, and a description whose round trip depends on nothing having a preference is",
        "one that cannot check itself."
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "input.extensions",
      "kind": "input",
      "as": "Extensions",
      "gives": "List",
      "of": {
        "type": "Int",
        "data": "Bytes"
      },
      "purpose": "One record per extension, in wire order. The data is octets: what is inside server_name or ALPN is a layer above this one."
    },
    {
      "id": "extensionType",
      "kind": "field",
      "as": "Extension Type",
      "form": {
        "of": "scalar",
        "octets": 2,
        "big": true,
        "signed": false
      },
      "about": "IANA's registry, which is open — 0 is server_name, 16 is ALPN, 0xff01 is renegotiation_info, and the next one is not in this file."
    },
    {
      "id": "evaluated.extensionType",
      "kind": "evaluated",
      "label": "which extension this is",
      "runs": "item.type",
      "gives": "Int"
    },
    {
      "id": "extensionLength",
      "kind": "field",
      "as": "Extension Length",
      "form": {
        "of": "scalar",
        "octets": 2,
        "big": true,
        "signed": false
      },
      "about": "Nought is a real answer and a common one. session_ticket, extended_master_secret and a server's acknowledgement of SNI are all present and empty, which means something quite different from being absent — and the only difference on the wire is four octets that say a name and nothing after them."
    },
    {
      "id": "evaluated.extensionLength",
      "kind": "evaluated",
      "label": "octets of extensionData",
      "runs": "held",
      "gives": "Int",
      "takes": {
        "held": "Int"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "extensionData",
      "kind": "field",
      "as": "Extension Data",
      "form": {
        "of": "opaque"
      },
      "about": "Uninterpreted, on purpose. §7.4.1.4 obliges a reader to ignore what it does not know, so a description that could only carry the extensions it had heard of would be a worse reader than the specification asks for."
    },
    {
      "id": "evaluated.extensionData",
      "kind": "evaluated",
      "label": "this extension's octets",
      "runs": "item.data",
      "gives": "Bytes"
    },
    {
      "id": "evaluated.extensionDataExtent",
      "kind": "evaluated",
      "label": "octets of extension, from the length",
      "runs": "len",
      "gives": "Int",
      "takes": {
        "len": "Int"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "moreSuites",
      "kind": "junction",
      "as": "another suite?",
      "about": "Sixteen octets of two-octet items, and nothing says eight. The reading asks where it is against where the length runs out, which is the same question a run of extensions asks and the same one a name's arcs ask in SNMP — the items being all one width here changes nothing about how the run ends."
    },
    {
      "id": "evaluated.moreSuites",
      "kind": "evaluated",
      "label": "another suite?",
      "runs": "position < at + wide + held",
      "gives": "Bool",
      "takes": {
        "at": "Int",
        "wide": "Int",
        "held": "Int"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "moreCompressions",
      "kind": "junction",
      "as": "another compression method?"
    },
    {
      "id": "evaluated.moreCompressions",
      "kind": "evaluated",
      "label": "another compression method?",
      "runs": "position < at + wide + held",
      "gives": "Bool",
      "takes": {
        "at": "Int",
        "wide": "Int",
        "held": "Int"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "moreExtensions",
      "kind": "junction",
      "as": "another extension?",
      "about": "The same question over items that are NOT all one width — an empty extension is four octets and ALPN's is eighteen. Which is why the bound is octets rather than a count: the description says where the run ends and the items say how far each of them got."
    },
    {
      "id": "evaluated.moreExtensions",
      "kind": "evaluated",
      "label": "another extension?",
      "runs": "position < at + wide + held",
      "gives": "Bool",
      "takes": {
        "at": "Int",
        "wide": "Int",
        "held": "Int"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "done",
      "kind": "end-parse",
      "as": "the end of a record",
      "about": "Where a reading may stop, which is when the extensions have spent their length and the record has spent its own. Stopping anywhere else is a record cut short."
    }
  ],
